<h3>55:46 — Theory dictation with the step numbers from this example</h3>
<p>He dictates (many repetitions for copying):</p>
<p>Whenever we are creating a child class object, the following sequence of events will be performed automatically as a part of instance control flow:</p>
<p>1. Identification of instance members from parent to child. *(this example: 4 to 14)*</p>
<p>2. Execution of instance variable assignments and instance blocks only in parent class. *(15 to 19)*</p>
<p>3. Execution of parent constructor. *(20)*</p>
<p>4. Execution of instance variable assignments and instance blocks in child class. *(21 to 26)*</p>
<p>5. Execution of child constructor. *(27)*</p>
<p>Then remaining Child.main print is 28.</p>
<pre class='code'>class Child extends Parent {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Child c = new Child(); // steps 4–27 happen here
        System.out.println(&quot;Child main&quot;); // 28
    }
}</pre>
<h3>59:50 — Copy the example, variable tracing, and numbers</h3>
<p>Long classroom pause. He says it is not that easy — compulsory clear clarity. Give the numbers appropriately. Mention child first instance block and child second instance block. Complete example: whenever we execute parent-to-child child class, what happens; whenever we create an object, what happens.</p>
<p>He restates steps while they write: execution of parent constructor; execution of instance variable assignments and instance blocks in child class.</p>
<h3>1:02:51 — Only child `main` runs; parent `main` does not</h3>
<p>Because we are executing child class, only child class `main` will be executed. Parent class main will not be executed.</p>
<p>Recall from last session (static / class loading):</p>
<ul><li>Whenever we are executing / loading child class, both parent and child classes are involved (static control flow of both).</li></ul>
<ul><li>Whenever we are executing parent, child class will not be loaded; child members are not required.</li></ul>
<pre class='code'>class Parent {
    static {
        System.out.println(&quot;Parent static&quot;);
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(&quot;Parent main&quot;);
    }
}
class Child extends Parent {
    static {
        System.out.println(&quot;Child static&quot;);
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(&quot;Child main&quot;);
    }
}
// java Child
// prints
// Parent static
// Child static
// Child main
// (Parent main is identified, never executed)
// java Parent
// prints
// Parent static
// Parent main
// (Child class not loaded)</pre>
<p>He tells them to finish numbers on the instance example.</p>
